item.nusmp.holy_handgrenade.card:
Legend Grade charm. Can be a Djinn's Metal Vessel. Four shalt thou not count, neither count thou two, excepting that thou then proceed to three. Five is right out. Once at the number three, being the third number be reached, then, lobbest thou thy Holy Hand Grenade of Antioch towards thy foe, who, being naughty in My sight, shall snuff it.
Passive. Tensura's Holy Attack Resistance is lent to you while it is worn.
Count to Three (hold the use button for 3 seconds, 5% of your existence points, 5 minute cooldown). The grenade is lobbed up to nine blocks where you look, and the d4+1 of the card is rolled:
 2: it does not explode (it clatters and is spent, the cooldown stands);
 3: it explodes in an eight block circle: every EVIL creature (hostile monsters, the undead, daemons; never a player) takes 99 holy damage, and every GOOD creature (you, your allies, pets and summons, villagers, golems) is healed 33 hit points; neutral creatures are untouched;
 4: nothing happens, the grenade stays in your hand and the existence points you spent come back;
 5: it explodes in your hand: 33 necrotic damage to every foe within five blocks and to you (this self-damage never kills: it always leaves you a heart).
Requires good alignment. A hand that has shed innocent blood (a villager, a player-made golem or somebody's pet killed in the last three days) is not trusted: it always rolls the five.
Tabletop made game: the 30 ft throw, 15 ft circle and the damage are kept (feet to blocks); the "good alignment" requirement became the blood-guilt mark; the damage to players is capped as everywhere in the relics.
